{"id": "EUVD-2026-103700", "enisaUuid": "31953308-bb41-3eed-b2af-7476d2dbdc0d", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nBluetooth: hci_sock: reject out-of-range OCF values\n\nThe raw HCI socket security filter has 128 OCF bits per supported OGF,\nbut masks the 10-bit OCF with 127 before looking up the command. An\nunprivileged socket can therefore submit a reserved OCF that aliases an\nallowlisted command modulo 128.\n\nA conforming controller should reject reserved opcodes. Nevertheless,\nthe security decision must apply to the opcode that will actually be\nsent, especially since controller-specific behavior is outside the host\nstack's control.\n\nReject OCF values that cannot be represented by the security filter\ninstead of aliasing them onto an unrelated command.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:15:09", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:19:57", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/70b0a27bdde0cb524349c8261202c7c9393cf5e9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/598686f5d65b9af2223ed9d22fadba16e09f6ca8", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c1fd465ea1c5aef459f9bc3ac602b5353e0f536f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/68f0bcc4e16e31ff8dbe6ca93116eb70d7b6ac44", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/320dedad15e8bbaecc8d2d7fd4189defb84caa85", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/173457fa3e99ef4188dd0fe63e4dee98d0e441a9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/47d67ec424e63e61e9eb58633d43a9d58a1852b6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e93fad891c72deb84cae49430163b384ebcc92b1"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98460", "GHSA-66xw-2cgj-6x3v"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.18, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "03f5e664-1753-3ed1-ba96-d00abf4cead9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "125190d2-2cca-3a71-956f-5e25c096afe5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <68f0bcc4e16e31ff8dbe6ca93116eb70d7b6ac44"}, {"id": "22339053-e03a-3b53-9b1c-8d29d143fdf9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <c1fd465ea1c5aef459f9bc3ac602b5353e0f536f"}, {"id": "268cc1d8-e05e-3a3a-862a-0683c1806d01", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.55"}, {"id": "4db63ce5-8dfd-3892-aa94-372d517ec5fd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2.6.12"}, {"id": "7b863594-60c3-3790-be9a-0f9527e77b39", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <47d67ec424e63e61e9eb58633d43a9d58a1852b6"}, {"id": "8405b80b-876a-377a-9b73-f348a12ffb00", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "9017f47a-5807-3a05-ad91-b40918155df1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.9"}, {"id": "9182e2af-acba-3f23-81f5-5c2b903a29f8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <320dedad15e8bbaecc8d2d7fd4189defb84caa85"}, {"id": "9927e2a2-d6e0-3d8a-b141-3bb6bd8e9aa0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.112"}, {"id": "9ec06aeb-015a-359e-a227-25bd935444c3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.10.271"}, {"id": "ab7d01b3-25f6-3e4a-8cc8-0bed854f511a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <173457fa3e99ef4188dd0fe63e4dee98d0e441a9"}, {"id": "bb5d9054-55bc-3b04-b3ac-c0396c6506d4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.158"}, {"id": "bb865d6d-2e96-3a8a-8a92-677ef1644100", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1